pve-csi-copy (0.3.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fix endpoint that never loaded: pvedaemon/pveproxy run `perl -T` (taint
    mode), which IGNORES both PERL5LIB and PERL5OPT. The 0.1.x/0.2.0 loader set
    exactly those via systemd Environment=, so it was inert — csi_copy_volume
    was never registered in the running daemons (an authenticated POST returned
    "Method ... not implemented"). The old verify passed regardless because it
    checked its OWN non-taint perl, never the live daemon.
  * Move the Perl module into a default @INC dir: /usr/share/perl5/PVECSICopy.pm
    and /usr/share/perl5/PVECSICopy/Impl.pm (was /usr/lib/pve-csi-copy/perl),
    loaded via a command-line `-MPVECSICopy` — the only mechanism taint mode
    honours.
  * Load it through a wrapper (/usr/lib/pve-csi-copy/pve-csi-copy-exec) called
    from each daemon's systemd ExecStart override, instead of a hardcoded perl
    command line. The wrapper reads the base unit's real ExecStart at start time
    and injects only `-MPVECSICopy`, so it survives a future PVE changing the
    daemon invocation, args, or perl flags — only a fundamental pve-manager
    restructure could affect it, and the live-daemon verify catches that loudly.
    It is deliberately fail-safe: on any problem (module hidden, shebang not
    perl, base command unreadable) it execs the daemon unmodified — a missing
    endpoint is acceptable, a dead pvedaemon/pveproxy is not.
  * Override ExecReload to a full `systemctl restart`: PVE's graceful reload is
    an in-process exec() that drops the command-line `-M`, so a plain reload
    would silently unload the endpoint. Converting the reload into a restart
    re-runs ExecStart (reloading the module) with no drop and no deadlock, and
    covers the pve-manager upgrade path (`deb-systemd-invoke
    reload-or-try-restart`). The fix is fully event-driven — no polling timer.
  * On successful registration the module now logs
    "pve-csi-copy: csi_copy_volume registered" to syslog, but only inside the
    daemons (guarded on $0), giving the verify a live signal.
  * pve-csi-copy-verify now gates on the LIVE running daemon: it requires a
    registration log for each of pvedaemon/pveproxy since its current start
    (correlated via ExecMainStartTimestamp), and keeps the module-compile /
    find_handler route check as a secondary structural assertion.
  * Handler logic, permissions, and volume/target validation are unchanged.

 -- CrunchyMonkies <opensource@crunchymonkies.invalid>  Wed, 22 Jul 2026 12:00:00 +0000

pve-csi-copy (0.2.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fix unreachable endpoint: move the copy method from
    PVE::API2::Storage::Content ('{volume}/copy') to PVE::API2::Storage::Status
    ('{storage}/csi-copy'). The content subtree is mounted with a
    fragment-joining, greedy '{volume}' path parameter, so PVE's router fed the
    whole 'content/<vol>/copy' suffix to the BUILT-IN root-only 'copy' method as
    volume='<vol>/copy' — observed on PVE 9.2.3 as a 400 "duplicate parameter
    (already defined in URI) with conflicting values!" (or a root@pam permission
    error without a body volume). The endpoint is now
    POST /nodes/{node}/storage/{storage}/csi-copy with the source volume as a
    body parameter; handler and permissions are unchanged.
  * Harden the target volume name: apply the same strict allow-list the source
    volume already uses (reject ':', '/', '..') instead of relying on the
    destination plugin's parse_volname to reject traversal on import, so the
    endpoint's safety no longer depends on a check in a separate code path.
  * pve-csi-copy-verify now asserts ROUTABILITY (find_handler, the same route
    resolution pveproxy uses), not just registration — the old check passed
    while the endpoint was unreachable.
  * Requires the migration controller / pvecsictl from the matching plugin
    release: the client now posts to the new URL.

 -- CrunchyMonkies <opensource@crunchymonkies.invalid>  Wed, 22 Jul 2026 00:00:00 +0000

pve-csi-copy (0.1.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Initial packaging of the token-authorised copy-volume endpoint for the
    proxmox-csi-plugin migration controller. Ships the self-contained Perl
    module tree, the pvedaemon/pveproxy loader drop-ins (managed by the
    maintainer scripts), and /usr/sbin/pve-csi-copy-verify.

